 184:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****     /**
 185:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * Function pointer for reading value from specified variable from Object Dictionary. If OD var
 186:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * buf, then this function must be called several times. After completed successful read functi
 187:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * If read is partial, it returns 'ODR_PARTIAL'. In case of errors function returns code simila
 188:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 189:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * Read can be restarted with @ref OD_rwRestart() function.
 190:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 191:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * At the moment, when Object Dictionary is initialized, every variable has assigned the same "
 192:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * default function simply copies data from Object Dictionary variable. Application can bind it
 193:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * for specific object. In that case application is able to calculate data for reading from own
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lenovo\AppData\Local\Temp\ccXm1HrZ.s 			page 21


 194:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * the moment of "read" function call. Own "read" function on OD object can be initialized with
 195:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * OD_extension_init() function.
 196:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 197:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * "read" function must always copy all own data to buf, except if "buf" is not large enough. (
 198:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * not return 'ODR_PARTIAL', if there is still space in "buf".)
 199:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 200:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @warning Do not use @ref CO_LOCK_OD() and @ref CO_UNLOCK_OD() macros inside the read() funct
 201:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * CO_critical_sections.
 202:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 203:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @param stream Object Dictionary stream object.
 204:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @param buf Pointer to external buffer, where to data will be copied.
 205:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @param count Size of the external buffer in bytes.
 206:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @param [out] countRead If return value is "ODR_OK" or "ODR_PARTIAL", then number of bytes su
 207:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * be returned here.
 208:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      *
 209:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      * @return Value from @ref ODR_t, "ODR_OK" in case of success.
 210:CANopen/301/CO_ODinterface.h ****      */
