  56:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * Error control and Emergency is used for control internal error state and for sending a CANopen E
  57:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  58:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * In case of error condition stack or application calls CO_errorReport() function with indication 
  59:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * Specific error condition is reported (with CANopen Emergency message) only the first time after 
  60:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * state of specific error condition is indicated by internal bitfield variable, with space for max
  61:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * CO_CONFIG_EM_ERR_STATUS_BITS_COUNT bits. Meaning for each bit is described by @ref CO_EM_errorSt
  62:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * error condition can be reset by CO_errorReset() function. In that case Emergency message is sent
  63:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * indication.
  64:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  65:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * Some error conditions are informative and some are critical. Critical error conditions set the c
  66:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * @ref CO_errorRegister_t. Critical error conditions for generic error are specified by @ref
  67:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * CO_CONFIG_ERR_CONDITION_GENERIC macro. Similar macros are defined for other error bits in in @re
  68:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  69:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * ### Emergency producer
  70:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * If @ref CO_CONFIG_EM has CO_CONFIG_EM_PRODUCER enabled, then CANopen Emergency message will be s
  71:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * any error condition. Emergency message contents are:
  72:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  73:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   Byte | Description
  74:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   -----|-----------------------------------------------------------
  75:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   0..1 | @ref CO_EM_errorCode_t
  76:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   2    | @ref CO_errorRegister_t
  77:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   3    | Index of error condition (see @ref CO_EM_errorStatusBits_t).
  78:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *   4..7 | Additional informative argument to CO_errorReport() function.
  79:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  80:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * ### Error history
  81:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * If @ref CO_CONFIG_EM has CO_CONFIG_EM_HISTORY enabled, then latest errors can be read from _Pre 
  82:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * (object dictionary, index 0x1003). Contents corresponds to bytes 0..3 from the Emergency message
  83:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  *
  84:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * ### Emergency consumer
  85:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * If @ref CO_CONFIG_EM has CO_CONFIG_EM_CONSUMER enabled, then callback can be registered by @ref
  86:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  * CO_EM_initCallbackRx() function.
  87:CANopen/301/CO_Emergency.h ****  */
